WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.231
Halo's 2.8× over TRL is not a kernel.

00:00:04.231 --> 00:00:05.862
The baseline is tuned.

00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:07.492
The asymmetry is sharding.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:14.740
The claim, from Halo's README: Halo delivers up to ~2.8× the training

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:20.415
throughput of stock TRL (2.7× at 25% less peak memory when

00:00:20.415 --> 00:00:22.478
both sides shard ZeRO-3).

00:00:22.478 --> 00:00:23.510
It holds.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:29.235
At 4k, Halo's throughput over stock TRL.

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:34.589
Halo at ZeRO-2, 2.80×; both at ZeRO-3, 1.25×.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.433
4k, batch 1, tok/s/GPU on 8 B300s.

00:00:40.433 --> 00:00:46.712
Halo, slow per-expert loop, 5,545; TRL, grouped GEMM, 3,885.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:52.991
Handicapped with the worse kernel, Halo is still ahead.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:59.820
The 2.8× is a real number about a real choice; the

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.918
1.25–2.68× is the framework.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:09.108
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
